From b1aef2903e410aad5b9b70f96ed8894cb47abff3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 19:31:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 54/75] wm: let the pinned config reach the activity without a
 PIP organizer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

moveActivityToPinnedRootTask pins the task but holds the activity at its
previous windowing mode, so the app does not relayout while the WM Shell
animates the shrink. The only code in the tree that lifts that override
again is PipTaskOrganizer's setActivityWindowingMode(.., UNDEFINED).

fydroid ships no WM Shell — ash owns the PIP window, its bounds and its
animation — so nothing ever cleared it. The activity never resolved to
WINDOWING_MODE_PINNED: isInPictureInPictureMode() stayed false,
onPictureInPictureModeChanged() never fired, and the stuck
mWaitForEnteringPinnedMode latch suppressed every visibility commit for
that activity.

Skip the deferral when no task organizer is registered and let the pinned
configuration cascade straight down. Gated on the organizer rather than on
an ARC flag so the upstream path is untouched wherever a shell exists.

First step of the PIP work; see device/fydeos/docs/picture-in-picture-plan.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I3d371bd7f50eddb533b57f8bdc4b42a2d55e5eda
---
 .../server/wm/RootWindowContainer.java        | 22 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/RootWindowContainer.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/RootWindowContainer.java
index a4e08dfb1e3b..a0c44451a7a3 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/RootWindowContainer.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/RootWindowContainer.java
@@ -2086,8 +2086,26 @@ class RootWindowContainer extends WindowContainer<DisplayContent>
             // Defer the windowing mode change until after the transition to prevent the activity
             // from doing work and changing the activity visuals while animating
             // TODO(task-org): Figure-out more structured way to do this long term.
-            r.setWindowingMode(intermediateWindowingMode);
-            r.mWaitForEnteringPinnedMode = true;
+            //
+            // fydroid-rt (ARC): this deferral holds the ACTIVITY at its previous
+            // windowing mode while the TASK becomes pinned, so the app does not
+            // relayout while the shell animates the shrink. The only code in the
+            // tree that ever lifts the override again is the WM Shell's
+            // PipTaskOrganizer (setActivityWindowingMode(.., UNDEFINED)).
+            //
+            // fydroid ships no WM Shell — ash owns the PIP window, its bounds and
+            // its animation — so with no task organizer registered nothing would
+            // clear it: the activity would never resolve to WINDOWING_MODE_PINNED,
+            // isInPictureInPictureMode() would stay false,
+            // onPictureInPictureModeChanged() would never fire, and the stuck
+            // mWaitForEnteringPinnedMode latch would suppress every visibility
+            // commit for the activity (see ActivityRecord#shouldApplyAnimation).
+            // With no organizer, let the pinned configuration cascade straight
+            // down to the activity instead.
+            if (mService.mTaskOrganizerController.getTaskOrganizer() != null) {
+                r.setWindowingMode(intermediateWindowingMode);
+                r.mWaitForEnteringPinnedMode = true;
+            }
             rootTask.forAllTaskFragments(tf -> {
                 if (!tf.isOrganizedTaskFragment()) {
                     return;
-- 
